# Angular security

- Never `bypassSecurityTrust*` on user-controlled input; avoid `[innerHTML]` with untrusted content; never build
  templates from user data; validate URLs before binding `[href]`.
- All HTTP through `HttpClient`, so auth, XSRF and error interceptors apply. Treat responses as `unknown` at the
  boundary when they are not from your own typed API.
- `environment.ts` is public: no secrets in it, no tokens in `localStorage`. Session cookies are httpOnly.
- Every authenticated or role-restricted route has a guard (`canMatch` for sensitive ones); the API enforces the same
  rule.
- Interceptors and logs never print tokens, personal data or response bodies.
- SSR: no server environment values in `TransferState` unless public; gate `window`/`document` with the platform.
- CSP is set server-side; no `unsafe-inline` in `script-src`.

